@startuml
title GET /api/oslfs/{address} — list a wallet's OSLF documents (headers, latest versions)
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Document owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "OslfsApiSdk\n.get()" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "OslfsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nread node" as Chain #FFE4A6

Owner -> SDK : get()
SDK -> SDK : address = privateKey\n  .getPublicKey().getAddress()
SDK -> API : GET /api/oslfs/{address}
API -> Domain : list(address)
Domain -> Chain : explore-deploy list.rho\n(registry env URI, address)
Chain --> Domain : OslfHeader[] or nothing
Domain --> API : Oslfs { oslfs }\n(empty list when the wallet has none)
API --> SDK : 200 Oslfs
SDK --> Owner : headers

note over Domain #FFF0C7
Headers carry id, version, created_at, name,
and description — not the query body. Fetch one
version to obtain the OSLF expression itself.
end note
@enduml
